<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating cumulative and tail probabilities for an exponential distribution</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The time \(X\) (in minutes) a customer waits at a bank counter in Mombasa follows an <b>exponential distribution</b> with \(\lambda = {@lam_str@}\). The mean waiting time is \({@mean_val@}\) minutes.</p>
<p>The cumulative probability formula for the exponential distribution is given by:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( P(X < x) = 1 - e^{-{@lam_str@}x} \quad \text{for } x \ge 0 \)</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Find the probability that a customer waits for <b>less than {@x_a@} minutes</b>.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an exact mathematical expression. For example, to enter \(1 - e^{-3}\), type <b>1 - e^(-3)</b> or <b>1 - exp(-3)</b>. Do not enter decimals).</i></p>
<p>\(P(X < {@x_a@}) =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Find the probability that a customer waits for <b>more than {@x_b@} minutes</b>.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an exact mathematical expression. For example, to enter \(e^{-3}\), type <b>e^(-3)</b> or <b>exp(-3)</b>).</i></p>
<p>\(P(X > {@x_b@}) =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Less Than Probability</b><br>
We substitute \(x = {@x_a@}\) directly into the cumulative probability formula:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X < {@x_a@}) = 1 - e^{-{@lam_str@} \times {@x_a@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X < {@x_a@}) = 1 - e^{-{@power_a@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(X < {@x_a@}) = {@ta1@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: More Than Probability</b><br>
The formula gives the probability of waiting <i>less</i> than \(x\) minutes. To find the probability of waiting <i>more</i> than \(x\) minutes, we must use the complement rule:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X > x) = 1 - P(X \le x) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X > {@x_b@}) = 1 - (1 - e^{-{@lam_str@} \times {@x_b@}}) \)</p>
<p>The \(1 - 1\) cancels out, leaving only the exponential term:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X > {@x_b@}) = e^{-{@lam_str@} \times {@x_b@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(X > {@x_b@}) = {@ta2@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
